[00:41.25]Hiding it, saying nothing — how fragile your eyes are
[00:51.25]They flush red — you liked me once, and that's enough
[01:03.55]Counting down the tenderness, the clock ticking on — don't take the kiss back
[01:19.35]One gust and I scatter — but you caught me
[01:31.35]Drifting through a lonely heart — are we lovers, or friends?
[01:45.05]Love needs no reason, like a kite that aches for the sky
[01:57.05]Maybe you understand me
[02:03.55]Love is like an hourglass — hold it tight and it still runs out
[02:14.20]In the corner of the classroom, holding each other — a hidden love like sparks
[02:27.90]Softly at my ear: stay and love me
[02:38.20]A paper plane draws an unfinished dream — your name is still here, in my hand